{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788809567929873001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"emblematic-apostolic-mouse","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"0a1145bc9d3d57066177f211ad9ad82666fa501544fa1336853fd12a9e7df6d9","event_uuid":"8e72fc2c-558b-4560-856c-0213e98aa2b6","position":{"commit_sha":"a39d59239b7ddb17445f1543a79be9646d8a6778","position":"1788807391056270761-8e72fc2c-558b-4560-856c-0213e98aa2b6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b808559f62bd6815a43d66c281d17a3d686d74c474a78ee33671d78b413c2e18","event_uuid":"6757c338-f14b-4cd8-a5f4-4672db95f5a4","position":{"commit_sha":"d06df22116ace4da5dab7522d74e085edfbf11c2","position":"1788807553823444419-6757c338-f14b-4cd8-a5f4-4672db95f5a4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e35ce45ae0d95cc3f63cda32c1d37402574c662aed33c06d1708ff61baca7b8e","event_uuid":"b1e140e2-47f4-48cd-92d5-bdbdf9f30f8b","position":{"commit_sha":"252e53654a9ff5dc14ca90ff77c94744b633dd3f","position":"1788807591197901375-b1e140e2-47f4-48cd-92d5-bdbdf9f30f8b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dd9a3a32680bfa01ebafecb228ba127dea228f168cd8b0ee1f69bc461a503d29","event_uuid":"d289277d-e48d-4477-8727-d8a1371c0db3","position":{"commit_sha":"e7c25f98ac886bfca69c5aa65e1702fda7e30bf3","position":"1788807678719142485-d289277d-e48d-4477-8727-d8a1371c0db3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"58e888270f86ff3c276ac18df7483ad0fa795d6eb0ecdd8e329e41426fc0679a","event_uuid":"54b2aa62-16b8-43fd-adbb-960f7be3b60e","position":{"commit_sha":"2598b9a4515859191f3c4afc66ce02de82d9303a","position":"1788807697091366617-54b2aa62-16b8-43fd-adbb-960f7be3b60e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Baseline maintenance: this story removes censused mechanism(s) `_one_engine_root` (autouse fixture, `tests/conftest.py:462-505`), the shadow-package bridge autouse fixture(s) in `tests/unit/conftest.py:22-97` (`_bridge_reconciler_shadow_package` / `_seed_dotted_namespace`), the engine-root autouse fixture(s) in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py:39-95`, and the `tests/_engine_path.py` test helper. Because `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` asserts the committed baseline equals the live tree, run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in the same change and commit `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (operator-sanctioned on the epic; precedent commit 81da792). State the sanction in the commit message.\n\nOrdering note: `--update-stale` refuses to write while anything is `new`, so apply the 29-key `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` → `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/reconciler/...` re-spell (next comment) first, then run `--update-stale` to drain the rows for the deleted fixtures and helper.","timestamp":1788807678719142485},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator sanction (recorded on the epic): this change carries a value-preserving key re-spell of the `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` keys in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (S2, 29 keys): prefix rewrite only, ceilings and counts unchanged; state this sanction in the commit message.","timestamp":1788807697091366617}],"created_at":1788807391056270761,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b1e140e2-47f4-48cd-92d5-bdbdf9f30f8b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bf96-5776-6a97-420f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nWith `rebar.reconciler` a real package (previous story), the shadow-package bridge, canonical-root guard, and key-seeding conftests are dead weight that still runs on every test, and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` keeps the retired name alive. The test-side loader complex is: `tests/_engine_path.py` (canonical-root helper: `engine_dir`, `acli_path`, `is_canonical_key`, `engine_root_of`, `foreign_engine_registrations`, `repo_root`), `tests/conftest.py:462-505` (`_one_engine_root` autouse), `tests/unit/conftest.py:22-97` (shadow-package bridge), `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py:39-95`, `tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_load_module_identity.py`, and `tests/_log_integrity.py:54` (`SHARED_LOGGER_NAMES` includes `rebar_reconciler`). 17 test files import `_engine_path` (`git grep -l _engine_path origin/main -- tests`). `pyproject.toml:691-698` has `testpaths=[\"tests\"]` and no `pythonpath`/`rootdir`, so the package rename needs no pytest config change. `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` has 29 `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` keys; a path move makes every one `new` and `make lint` fails. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\n1. Delete `tests/_engine_path.py`: its engine functions (`engine_dir`, `acli_path`, `is_canonical_key`, `engine_root_of`, `foreign_engine_registrations`) go with no replacement, the 17 importers are re-pointed, and the `repo_root()` callers fold onto `tests/_repo_root.py`.\n2. Delete `tests/conftest.py:462-505` (`_one_engine_root`), the `tests/unit/conftest.py:22-97` shadow bridge (keep the session-log fixture), and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py:39-95` (keep the two autouse env fixtures). Delete `tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_load_module_identity.py`.\n3. `tests/_log_integrity.py:54`: `SHARED_LOGGER_NAMES` becomes `(\"rebar\",)`; update `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py` to match.\n4. `git mv tests/unit/rebar_reconciler tests/unit/reconciler` and `git mv tests/integration/rebar_reconciler tests/integration/reconciler`; update `scripts/check_docs_index.py:43` and the docs that name the test path (`docs/coverage.md`, `docs/code-navigation.md`).\n5. `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`: re-spell the 29 `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` keys to `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/reconciler/...` with counts unchanged (operator-sanctioned maintenance edit, recorded on the epic and restated in the commit message). Do the re-spell first; then, because the deleted autouse fixtures and the deleted `tests/_engine_path.py` helper are censused mechanisms and `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` asserts the committed baseline equals the live tree, run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` (it refuses to write while anything is `new`) and commit the baseline in the same change (itemised in this ticket's comments).\n\n## Scope\n`tests/_engine_path.py` (deleted), `tests/conftest.py`, `tests/unit/conftest.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/**` (renamed), `tests/integration/reconciler/**` (renamed), `tests/_log_integrity.py`, `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py`, `tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py` (deleted), `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_load_module_identity.py` (deleted), `scripts/check_docs_index.py`, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, `docs/coverage.md`, `docs/code-navigation.md`. Out of scope: every `src/` file, the pytest configuration in `pyproject.toml` (no change needed), and the behaviour of any test beyond how it locates the engine.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `pytest tests/unit/reconciler -q -n 4 --dist worksteal` and `make test`. Edge: `pytest --co -q | grep -c rebar_reconciler` is 0; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` prints `new=0`; a non-editable install lane (`uv pip install .` then `pytest tests/unit/reconciler/apply -q`) passes — the dual-copy hazard that bug `ethnic-rubber-shoveler` (`bd2d-3e31-31d9-4a66`) guarded is gone because tests import the installed package like every other `rebar.*` test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No `tests/**/rebar_reconciler` directory; no `_one_engine_root`, `_bridge_reconciler_shadow_package`, `_seed_dotted_namespace` symbol — `git ls-tree` and `git grep`.\n- [ ] `tests/_engine_path.py` is absent and `git grep -n _engine_path -- tests` is empty.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` prints `new=0`.\n- [ ] `tests/_log_integrity.SHARED_LOGGER_NAMES == (\"rebar\",)` — `tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py` updated and green.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_engine_path.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"delete _one_engine_root"},{"path":"tests/unit/conftest.py","reason":"delete shadow bridge"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/","reason":"renamed package"},{"path":"tests/integration/reconciler/","reason":"renamed"},{"path":"tests/_log_integrity.py","reason":"one shared root"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py","reason":"SHARED_LOGGER_NAMES == (\"rebar\",)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_load_module_identity.py","reason":"delete"},{"path":".github/mechanism-baseline.json","reason":"29 keys re-spelled; deleted-fixture rows drained with --update-stale"},{"path":"scripts/check_docs_index.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/coverage.md","reason":"test path"},{"path":"docs/code-navigation.md","reason":"test path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","bf96-5776-6a97-420f"],["parent","ebf5-5d21-0124-4313"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"4b2a-e417-30ed-4f3a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Delete the test-side engine-root machinery and rename tests/unit/rebar_reconciler to tests/unit/reconciler","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8e72fc2c-558b-4560-856c-0213e98aa2b6","6757c338-f14b-4cd8-a5f4-4672db95f5a4","b1e140e2-47f4-48cd-92d5-bdbdf9f30f8b","d289277d-e48d-4477-8727-d8a1371c0db3","54b2aa62-16b8-43fd-adbb-960f7be3b60e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788809567929873001,"uuid":"bd2fe4c8-860f-40b0-867c-6c5fd1b804a1"}